---
/**
 * /tutorial/: the reader's map to the three annotated walks. Who the walks are
 * for, in what order to read them and how long each run takes, then the cards.
 *
 * Run times come from the `runtime` frontmatter of each walk, which quotes the
 * wall-clock gate in that program's committed output.txt.
 */
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import PageShell from '../../components/nav/PageShell.astro';
import { Code } from 'astro:components';
import { rustDark, rustLight } from '../../../shiki-rust-themes.mjs';
import { GITHUB_URL, MACHINE } from '../../consts';

const SHIKI = { light: rustLight, dark: rustDark };

const cloneCmd = `git clone https://github.com/deepcausality-rs/deep_causality.git
cd deep_causality`;

const title = 'Tutorial | DeepCausality CFD';
const description =
  'Three annotated walks through committed programs that fly a reentry descent through plasma blackout, tabulate its weather and land it under a retro burn.';

const stages = (await getCollection('tutorial')).sort(
  (a, b) => a.data.stage - b.data.stage
);

// Each runtime string opens with the measured seconds ("45.9 s against a 600 s budget").
const seconds = stages.map((s) => parseFloat(s.data.runtime));
const totalSeconds = seconds.reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0);
const totalMinutes = (totalSeconds / 60).toFixed(1);
const runList = seconds.map((s) => `${s.toFixed(1)} s`);
const runText = runList.length > 1 ? `${runList.slice(0, -1).join(', ')} and ${runList[runList.length - 1]}` : runList.join('');

const FAMILY_URL = `${GITHUB_URL}/tree/main/examples/avionics_examples/cfd/plasma_blackout`;
---
<PageShell title={title} description={description} path="/tutorial/">
  <header class="doc-head">
    <p class="eyebrow">Tutorial</p>
    <h1>Reading the plasma-blackout programs</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Three annotated walks through programs that fly a reentry descent through blackout, when the
      vehicle’s own plasma cuts off GPS. They tabulate the weather it flies in and land it under a
      retro burn.
    </p>
  </header>

  <section class="doc-sec" id="who">
    <h2>Who is this for, and how long does it take?</h2>
    <dl class="deflist">
      <div>
        <dt>Who</dt>
        <dd>
          A Rust programmer who wants to see a whole pause-and-fork study written out. No CFD or
          reentry background is needed. The walks explain the physics only where a design decision
          depends on it.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Order</dt>
        <dd>
          Walk 1, then 2, then 3. Walk 2 writes <code>weather_table.csv</code> and walk 3 reads it.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Run time</dt>
        <dd>
          {runText}: {totalMinutes} minutes in all, measured on {MACHINE}. Start each run
          first and read while it finishes.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>You need</dt>
        <dd>A Rust toolchain and a clone of the repository.</dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
    <Code code={cloneCmd} lang="bash" themes={SHIKI} />
    <p>
      Every number in the walks comes from that program’s committed <code>output.txt</code>.
      Compare your run against it; the wall-clock times will differ.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="doc-sec" id="walks" data-rise>
    <h2>The three walks</h2>

    <ol class="pipeline">
      {stages.map((s) => (
        <li class="pstage rise" style={`--i:${s.data.stage - 1}`}>
          <a class="panel corner-brackets pcard" href={`/tutorial/${s.id.replace(/^en\//, '')}/`}>
            <div class="pmain">
              <h3 class="ptitle">{s.data.title}</h3>
              <p class="pq">{s.data.question}</p>
              <p class="pio-row"><span class="k">You learn</span> {s.data.objective}</p>
              <p class="pio-row"><span class="k">Produces</span> {s.data.produces}</p>
              <p class="pmeta num">{s.data.runtime}.</p>
            </div>
            <span class="pgo" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          </a>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ol>

    <p class="next-links">
      <a href={FAMILY_URL}>Source for all three programs <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="doc-sec" id="after">
    <h2>What can you do after the third walk?</h2>
    <p>
      Open an unfamiliar <code>CfdFlow</code> program and answer four questions about it:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Where its leg boundaries sit, and why there.</li>
      <li>
        Whether its what-if (an alternative continued from a pause) forks a paused state or changes
        the world.
      </li>
      <li>What its gates would catch. A gate is a pass or fail check on a result.</li>
      <li>Which of its constants record a measurement, not a preference.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="doc-sec" id="subject">
    <h2>What do the programs simulate?</h2>
    <p>
      A reentry vehicle whose plasma sheath cuts every GNSS (satellite navigation) link. It
      navigates on inertial sensors through the dark, then lands under a retro burn. The problem
      needs fluid dynamics, plasma chemistry, navigation and control to be right at once. The NASA
      CFD Vision 2030 Study names that multidisciplinary coupling as an open challenge, and the
      <a href="/why/">Why page</a> maps it in full.
    </p>
  </section>
</PageShell>

<style>
  .pipeline { list-style: none; margin: 0 0 var(--space-4); padding: 0; max-width: none; display: grid; gap: var(--space-4); }
  /* The connector: what one walk produces, the next consumes. */
  .pstage + .pstage { position: relative; margin-top: var(--space-4); }
  .pstage + .pstage::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    top: calc(-1 * var(--space-4) - var(--space-2));
    left: var(--space-6);
    width: 1px;
    height: calc(var(--space-4) + var(--space-2) * 2);
    background: var(--line-2);
  }

  .pcard {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr auto;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    align-items: start;
    padding: var(--space-5);
    color: var(--fg-0);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-1);
    transition: border-color var(--dur-fast) var(--ease-out),
                background-color var(--dur-fast) var(--ease-out);
  }
  .pcard:hover {
    border-color: var(--line-2);
    background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 5%, transparent);
  }
  .pmain { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--space-2); min-width: 0; }
  .pmain p { margin: 0; }
  .ptitle { font-weight: var(--fw-heading); font-size: var(--t-h4); line-height: var(--lh-h4); }
  .pq { color: var(--fg-1); font-size: var(--t-body-sm); max-width: var(--measure); }
  .pio-row { color: var(--fg-1); font-size: var(--t-body-sm); }
  .pio-row .k {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--t-eyebrow);
    letter-spacing: var(--ls-eyebrow);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--fg-2);
    margin-right: var(--space-2);
  }
  .pmeta { color: var(--fg-2); font-size: var(--t-eyebrow); margin-top: var(--space-1); }
  .pgo { align-self: center; }
  .pgo::after {
    content: '→';
    display: inline-block;
    color: var(--accent);
    transition: transform var(--dur-fast) var(--ease-out);
  }
  .pcard:hover .pgo::after { transform: translateX(2px); }

  .doc-sec :global(pre.astro-code) { max-width: none; }
</style>
